Seeds OpenSSL's random numbers on Radix with getentropy(), as on WASI:
the C library has it, and the kernel's random numbers behind it. The
weak reference OpenSSL tries first finds nothing in a static program
that nothing else links getentropy into, and the devices it would read
next are a fallback. The change is under OpenSSL's Apache-2.0 license,
so that it can go upstream as it is.

--- a/providers/implementations/rands/seeding/rand_unix.c
+++ b/providers/implementations/rands/seeding/rand_unix.c
@@ -395,7 +395,7 @@
     return getrandom(buf, buflen, 0);
 #  elif (defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__NetBSD__)) && defined(KERN_ARND)
     return sysctl_random(buf, buflen);
-#  elif defined(__wasi__)
+#  elif defined(__wasi__) || defined(__radix__)
     if (getentropy(buf, buflen) == 0)
       return (ssize_t)buflen;
     return -1;
